{"prototypeToken":{"displayName":20,"displayBars":20,"flags":{"pf2e":{"linkToActorSize":true,"autoscale":true}},"height":1,"width":1,"name":"Meatmonger","actorLink":false,"texture":{"src":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-su-pf2e/art/tokens/meatmonger.webp","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"bar1":{"attribute":"attributes.hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":null},"light":{"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1},"negative":false,"priority":0},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false,"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":true,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-su-pf2e/art/subjects/meatmonger.webp"}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"depth":1},"name":"Meatmonger","type":"npc","effects":[],"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":160,"temp":0,"max":160,"details":""},"ac":{"value":21,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":30,"otherSpeeds":[],"details":"meat cart"},"weaknesses":[{"type":"cold-iron","value":5,"exceptions":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["common","fey","jotun","necril"],"details":""},"level":{"value":6},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Meatmongers are gregarious fey merchants who peacefully sell delectable and occasionally dubious meat from their large wooden carts... except when they're low on stock!</p>\n<p>A meatmonger has a simple need to serve delicious meats to clients. But a meatmonger's client can never be sure exactly what kind of meat they are eating. Many people have taken to cannibalism because of a meatmonger. And many more have fallen victim to the meatmonger's need for new ingredients.</p>\n<p>Meatmongers don't shy away from selling their wares to unscrupulous individuals either. It's not uncommon to find one peddling their goods to a gang of trolls or the hungry dead.</p>\n<h2>No Meat For You</h2>\n<p>The meatmonger does not barter and only accepts coins for its goods. Hungry families who try to trade one of their own for a meal will find the meatmonger giving them the cold shoulder—no, not the one in the cart. It is willing to pay for services rendered, though. Meatmongers are always looking for delectable spices and marinades, as well as blacksmiths to sharpen their blades. As a bonus to the income earned, meatmongers do not usually butcher those they find helpful.</p>\n<h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2>\n<p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 30/65/125 gp</p>\n<p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> armor (light, medium), perception item, skill items (Athletics, Crafting, Diplomacy, Lore [Cooking])</p>\n<p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> bane, charisma, constitution, energy resistant (positive), evil, lawful, strength, wild</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Strange and Unusual","authors":"Juho Kattelus","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"creatureType":""},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.932,"previous":{"schema":0.853,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":5},"dex":{"mod":2},"con":{"mod":5},"int":{"mod":2},"wis":{"mod":4},"cha":{"mod":4}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":14,"senses":[{"type":"scent","acuity":"imprecise","range":60}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":17,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":11,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":14,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"athletics":{"base":15},"crafting":{"base":13},"diplomacy":{